						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Friday, April 20, 2001</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Huzzah and Bravo </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Night Raiders, lvl 1 - 20
Nomad lvl 20 - 50 are pleased to announce their Uber guild Apex will soon be formed to continued the Norrath tradition of assistence and kindness on a higher level.
							<br>
							 - Elizah<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=140">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=140">[View Comments]</a>



					<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Friday, April 13, 2001</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Solusek Message Boards!! </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Sorry everyone... I'd have thought someone would have sent this to you by now...

www.solusekro.org went down when Northpoint Communictions closed up shop.

They are currently up at:
http://209.202.194.157

Unfortuately they are having problems getting the DNS straightened out... but if you go to the above IP address you can connect right in...

None of the messages/boards were lost!

Hope to be back to normal soon.


(Just relaying this info... I'm not directly involved in the running of the board... Just one of the moderators)

Zerion Silverthorn
							<br>
							 - Zerion Silverthorn<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=139">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><BR><img src=images/redline.gif height=2 width="100%"><BR><BR></TD></TR>
					

						<TR><TD><p class="pTitle">Plane of Fear </p></TD></TR>
							<TR><TD><p class=pText>
							Obsidian Fear shall be invading The Plane of Fear with some members of DarkBlood & Wrath of Vaer. We have scheduled this event to take place on May 19-21. 
Adrastea Trailtracker
							<br>
							 - Adrastea<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=138">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Wednesday, April 11, 2001</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Message Boards </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Sorry I haven't got back with most of you about the message boards. I have no idea what happened to them, since I do not run them. I only link to them. Although, with enough response I may put some more up on my own. Give us some feedback on that issue. In the meantime, you can easily post raids and such in the news here. Thanks!
							<br>
							 - Anumatu<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=135">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=135">[View Comments]</a>



					<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Monday, April 09, 2001</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Lightbringers Recruiting! </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							    Greetings Norrath! The Lightbringers of Ro located on the Solusek Ro server are now recruiting!  We are dedicated to the cooperative gain of experience, being nice, and helping out others in need when we can.  If you'd like to join our growing family please visit our web site for more information: http://on.to/lor


							<br>
							 - Mijit<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=134">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Friday, April 06, 2001</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Anarchy Slayers </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							 A well establish giuld called Anarchy Slayers is currently looking for new members. Requierments are must be lvl 10 and above, wor goud in groups and iin soloing and have a joy foragood slaying here and there. If intersted tap a slayer on the shoulders and tell them you want to join up.



							<br>
							 - Cubiche<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=133">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Thursday, April 05, 2001</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Lords of Solusek </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							The guild Lords of Solusek has been created after much waiting. If you are interested in joining and are level 10 to 20 please send Alberad a tell. Everyone have a great time playing EverQuest =)
							<br>
							 - Alberad<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=132">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Wednesday, April 04, 2001</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">RPGwear.com News Release </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							-------------------

RPGwear, an officially licensed provider of EverQuest apparel, is pleased to
announce a partnership with Blair Grafix.

Blair Grafix, a team of renowned artists commissioned by the film industry
for its artwork, will work with RPGwear to produce high quality artwork to
be featured on RPGwear products. Blair Grafix is well-known for work such as
Elf Lord, Elf Quest, Sno, Dick Sweenie, and countless other projects during
the past 30 years. Barry Blair, the owner of Blair Grafix, says "We are
looking forward to this joint venture."

The first combined efforts of Blair Grafix and RPGwear have resulted in a
design that will be featured on the event shirt for the upcoming EverQuest
Fan Faire in San Diego. In addition, RPGwear is releasing the "Druid" shirt,
the first in a series of 14 class-related shirts, and will begin offering
several new posters featuring Blair Grafix artwork.

"We are very excited to have Barry and his team on our side. Their work is
very stunning and I think it meets the quality of work we produce. I invite
you to stop by and see for yourself, I am sure you will agree as I do that
they are masters at doing something they love." says Cory Rafiner, President
and CEO of RPG Inc.

RPGwear will be offering its merchandise at the Fan Faire in San Diego. Make
sure you stop by and talk with the staff and share your thoughts and ideas.

These designs along with many others are available at www.RPGwear.com. 

RPG, Inc.

-----------------


							<br>
							 - Be0wulf@rpgwear.com<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=131">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
